      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND AND PURPOSE",
          "content": "This study determined the test-retest reliability of measurements of responses to posteroanterior (PA) forces made using a recently developed instrument."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SUBJECT",
          "content": "Twenty-two subjects with nonspecific low back pain participated."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "The length of the low- stiffness or \"toe\" region and the slope of the linear portion of the force-displacement curve were measured on two occasions. Reliability of repeated measurements was evaluated by intraclass correlation coefficients and percentage-of-agreement scores. The presence of a systematic change in the response to PA forces was evaluated by a paired-samples t test."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "High reliability coefficients were obtained for both indices of the response to PA forces. The t test revealed no systematic change with repeated testing."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION AND DISCUSSION",
          "content": "The new device provides highly reliable measurement of the lumbar PA force-displacement relationship and may prove useful in evaluating theories that have suggested a relationship between spinal symptoms and abnormal PA stiffness."
        }
      ]},
